<title>SINGAPORE: Shell Singapore says cracker output at 50 percent.</title>
<headline>Shell Singapore says cracker output at 50 percent.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Singapore confirmed the partial shutdown of a 10,000 tonne a day cracking unit on December 7 which has caused a production loss of 5,000 tonnes a day, a company spokeswoman said on Monday.</p>
<p>The thermal gas oil unit which was closed due to a leak in a furnace, is expected to be shut for about one week, she said.</p>
<p>The unit cracks heavy residual fuel to produce between 30 and 40 percent of middle distillate and fuel oil making up the rest.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
</text>
